UPDATE public.listing_translations SET title='2-Storey Pool House, Ban Suan Suwattana', description='Property details

Two-storey detached house with swimming pool, number 38/197, Ban Suan Suwattana Phase 1, Soi 12, Noen Phlap Wan Road, Nong Prue, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri. One Chanote title, 91288, covers 133 sq.wah (532 sq.m.). SAM lists four bedrooms and five bathrooms. Announced sale price THB 6,920,000; asset 3A0852.

Material access issue: the village road is private, with approximately six metres of concrete carriageway and eight metres of right of way. SAM describes access title 100619, parcel 1763, as private land intentionally divided for open access. Title 20098, parcel 731, is road land within the project''s subdivision.

Exterior/pool photos display 16 March 2022, and porch/interior photos display 28 February 2024. Nineteen source images are retained. The pool photo shows an empty pool and vegetation around it; inspect current pool structure, filtration, leakage and house condition. Pool operability is not confirmed.

Location and access

Source-listed nearby places include Ban Noen Phlap Wan School, Sawang Boriboon Wittaya School and Wat Sutthawat Nong Prue. From Si Racha toward Sattahip on Sukhumvit Road, pass HomePro North Pattaya, Boonthavorn and Index Living Mall Pattaya, turn left into Sukhumvit 53, cross the railway-side road into Noen Phlap Wan Road, pass Darul Abror Mosque, then left into Ban Suan Suwattana for approximately 140 metres and left into the internal road; the property is ahead.

Property notes

Rectangular plot with an eastern side approximately 24 metres wide, of which only approximately four metres fronts the road, and depth approximately 22 metres. SAM''s registered acquisition lists the two-storey house numbered 38/197 and swimming pool. SAM reports orange planning zoning.

SAM states that the sale plot is not within the original subdivision approval: it was subdivided later within the project and has long used the subdivision road. Verify access-right evidence over both road plots, boundaries and actual use before offering. Long use is not presented here as proof of registered easement or rights equivalent to original subdivision plots.

